WEBVTT

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.860
That was great.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.340
Since the first time I ever saw a play...

00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:16.270
...I've always just...

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:23.520
"Kokone is my life"

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:21.620
Her singing was great, as always.

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.050
She's going to debut as a singer in no time.

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:28.020
I've just yearned to do that.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:32.790
At one time, man was one with the world of truth.

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:38.270
But the written word brought forth prosperity and suffering.

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:47.480
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin,'</i> <i>you're a divine crown</i>

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:53.480
<i>The kanji for "love" and "grief " look very similar</i>

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:58.890
<i>When I realized that, dawn suddenly broke</i>

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:04.660
<i>The air was filled with so much</i> <i>silence that "blue" "fought"</i>

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:11.000
<i>When suddenly you slid in to the right of me</i>

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.900
<i>Rippling with a clatter</i>

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:16.840
<i>and tangled in red thread</i>

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:21.740
<i>and a 39-degree fever of passion</i>

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:27.180
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin,'</i> <i>you're a divine crown</i>

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:33.250
<i>A crown worn on high with pride</i>

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:38.690
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin,'</i> <i>"soothe" my hidden "heart below"</i>

00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:44.700
<i>Its form is too much to handle right now</i>

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:47.640
<i>God's wisdom, the "h" in "her"</i>

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.370
<i>With a tearful, feverish gaze</i>

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:53.310
<i>let's stand side by side</i> <i>and look at tomorrow's moon</i>

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:56.140
<i>(Let's stand side by side</i> <i>and look at tomorrow's moon)</i>

00:01:56.140 --> 00:02:03.550
<i>The things you can do are so striking</i>

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:11.990
"Reach Them! My True Voice"

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:11.990
A play? Not a dramatic reading?

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:15.800
Yes! The Verbalism Club's
Outdoor Theater Performance!

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:13.500
"Setting Up

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:13.500
Please wait juuust a little longer."

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.130
"Verbalism Club Outdoor Stage Performance

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.130
'Hanako and Princess Kaguya'"

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:17.500
Thanks to our negotiations,

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:22.070
we can use Asagaya's
Shinmei Shrine's Noh theater.

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:25.170
Here're your radical new scripts!

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:27.680
"Radical"? Who even uses that word anymore?

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.580
Suspicion that Sakurako lies about her age is on the rise!

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:34.210
Ta-da! We're announcing everyone's roles!

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:37.350
"Title: 'Hanako and Princess Kaguya'"

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:40.050
"Roles

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:40.050
Hanako / Akira

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:40.050
Princess Kaguya / Maia

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:40.050
Grandma / Tsutomu

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:40.890
What?!

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:41.990
Prince / Hayato

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:41.990
Kappa / Karan

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:41.990
Theme Song / Kokone"

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:42.890
Th-The theme song?

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:44.490
There's no savior!

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:46.930
Hey, what country is
Princess Kaguya the princess of?

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:49.660
I'm the grandma? Not a prince?!

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:52.870
No! No! I don't wanna be a kappa!
I wanna be a princess!

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:54.440
--I object!!
--I object!

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:55.670
"Princess Kaguya / Maia

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:55.670
Grandma / Tsutomu

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:55.670
Prince / Hayato

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:55.670
Kappa / Karan

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:55.670
Theme Song / Kokone"

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.670
Calm down, both of you.

00:02:55.670 --> 00:02:58.870
--Be quiet, Big Brother!
--Put a sock in it, "Prince"!

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:03.080
U-Um... I'm just singing?

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:06.710
Yes. Your song will give the stage some color.

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:09.420
It's a big responsibility, you know.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:12.520
I see...

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:14.190
Manager.

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:17.290
I have to play the role of the sage who was once the savior.

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:20.200
Huh? Was there a sage in this?

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.030
What about Hanako?

00:03:22.030 --> 00:03:24.370
Kikogami should play her.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:27.370
Why are you having Akira crossdress, anyway?

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:29.970
Boys in drag have a certain appeal to them, don't you think?

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:33.540
I disagree. It's too soon for
Kikogami to take a lead role.

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:35.700
We should ask her how she feels about it.

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:38.900
Well?

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:45.650
I... rather than sing... I'd like to act!

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:48.150
Please, let me!

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:50.660
Okay, it's decided!

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:54.290
Practice hard between now and the main event this weekend.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.160
This weekend?!

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:01.930
"Shinmei Shrine"

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:01.930
"Hanako and Princess Kaguya"

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:08.080
Come get your full-length sausages to enjoy along with the play.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.180
We have photos of the
Verbalism Club members,

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:13.180
as well as goods they've made by hand themselves.

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:16.820
Now, the daytime part of the Verbalism Club's play,

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:20.460
"Verbalism Club Outdoor Stage Performance

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:20.460
'Hanako and Princess Kaguya'"

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:21.160
"Hanako and Princess Kaguya," will now begin.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:27.760
Grandma, what do you mean there's a letter for me?

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:31.600
Grandma, what do you mean there's...

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:36.030
No matter what happens, we'll cover for you.

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:42.180
A-Are you not confident I-I can do this?

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:44.550
It's not just you.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:47.650
Actually, it's Kaibuki that has me the most worried.

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:52.120
I am the one they call the savior sage.

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:55.320
I reside in the mountains cutting bamboo

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:57.690
as I bring salvation to the people of this world.

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:59.890
Thank goodness.

00:04:59.890 --> 00:05:03.300
For the love of...! He's already throwing in unwanted ad libs!

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.800
I see. So it's okay to just ignore the script.

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:07.170
Of course it isn't!

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:08.800
But they're loving it!

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:12.140
Grandma, what do you mean...

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:16.640
Grandma... Grand... ma...

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:21.520
Hanako! Hanako, where are you, dearie?

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:22.720
I am here!

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:24.490
Oh, Hanako!

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:27.320
G-G-Grandma!

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:32.890
What do you mean... there is a letter for me?

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:35.760
"Kokone is my life"

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:35.760
Kokone...

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:37.270
Not good...

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:38.770
Hang in there, Kokone!

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:43.040
Oh, Hanako. Today is a fine day for saving people, isn't it?

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:49.270
Wh-Why, yes, G-Grandpa.
The weather is very good...

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:54.920
No way.

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:56.750
Is this a joke?

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:01.520
She was able to do it during practice...

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:04.930
"Kokone is my life"

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:04.060
Kokone!

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:05.360
Do your best!

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:11.070
H-Here, Hanako, I have a letter for you from the princess of the moon.

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:15.800
The moon? And it's for m-m-me...

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:18.360
Um, well...

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:25.480
The messiah of the moon

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:27.810
is your elder sister.

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:31.220
He's ad-libbing again!

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:33.320
Princess Kaguya is a messiah?

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:35.890
I see! So I was a savior, too!

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:37.380
No!

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:42.060
Until you reach your sixteenth birthday,

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:44.970
raising you here on Earth

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:49.440
has been the savior sage's duty!

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:52.600
Akira is covering for me.

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:59.070
Y-Yes! I-In order to meet my sister...

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:16.360
...I-I must go to the m-moon...

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:19.270
I can't hear you!

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:25.210
Kokone is trying her best!

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:27.610
Her songs at Shirobaco are the best!

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:29.610
Gentlemen, I'll ask you to come with me.

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:31.150
What are you doing to me?!

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:33.310
This is a total mess.

00:07:33.310 --> 00:07:36.320
This is why I said it was too soon for her!

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:40.650
Go to the moon, Hanako!
In order to learn about this world!

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:48.620
Y-Yes. I-I will go to the moon.

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:51.870
"On Break

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:51.870
Wait just a little while for

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:51.870
the evening performance."

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:58.540
We should reduce Kokone's lines and spread them out to other people.

00:07:58.540 --> 00:07:59.540
Why?

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:02.140
The play won't work as-is.

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:04.480
Tsutomu and Karan, you're fine with it, right?

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:06.380
Well, it's not like we have much choice.

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:08.320
Yeah, let's do that.

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:10.590
We aren't the ones who should decide that.

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:12.420
Am I wrong?

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:17.020
Not everyone can do things in a single bound like you.

00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:19.930
Do you want to make Kikogami embarrass herself further?

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:27.360
U-Um... I'm heading out for a bit!

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:33.110
That was a little harsh, don'tcha think?

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:36.180
Hayato, that's one demerit point.

00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:39.550
There are times when excessive kindness can hurt others.

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:45.520
Like, not being able to say your lines is preschool level stuff!

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:47.920
They're nothing special, huh?

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:52.030
"Hanako and Princess Kaguya"

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:52.030
Even with a pretentious name like the Verbalism Club.

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:55.900
Because of me... they're criticizing everyone.

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:03.140
That candy is red. A, E, I, O, U.

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:06.110
There are shrimp swimming in the seaweed.

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:10.950
Prince...

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:14.750
Y-Y-You're very...

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:21.780
Why... can't I say it?

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:36.760
Akira?

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:39.670
The insects are talking.

00:09:39.670 --> 00:09:41.610
The insects?

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:51.350
You're... right... It's such a pretty... sound...

00:09:51.350 --> 00:10:00.330
Even though they're small...
You can hear the insects' noises...

00:10:00.330 --> 00:10:01.820
It's not just noise.

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:15.940
A leaf bunny?

00:10:15.940 --> 00:10:18.140
Listen closely.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:27.620
Verbalize.

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:29.520
Rejoice.

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:32.190
I shall now set you free.

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:54.920
The prince is a t-total hottie.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:57.650
Hanako, go on the attack!

00:10:57.650 --> 00:10:59.090
Now, Prince.

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:03.560
Bring me truffles from the finest of chocolatiers!

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:06.890
Yes, Princess Kaguya.
I will gladly bring them for you.

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:10.190
B-But, Prince...

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:14.500
My sister and you...

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:18.070
--...w-will be g-getting married...
--Ouch. This is even worse than during the day.

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:21.440
--...the m-messenger said...
--Maybe it really was too early for her.

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:23.740
What's up?

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:26.740
The sound of the wind... vanished.

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:33.020
"Hanako and Princess Kaguya"

00:11:33.350 --> 00:11:35.790
Hey, how long do we have to watch this?

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:37.290
Huh? What'd you say?

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:38.760
I said...!

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:41.130
Are you just going to give up, kappa?

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:44.530
Hanako! Hanako! Steal his love, kappa!

00:11:44.530 --> 00:11:47.900
It's not too late, kappa!

00:11:47.900 --> 00:11:53.240
I-I won't... I-let you have the prince!

00:11:56.580 --> 00:12:00.280
The customers suddenly got real quiet.

00:12:07.590 --> 00:12:10.490
What? Why now?

00:12:09.260 --> 00:12:11.250
"M.J.B.K. Detected Contact us ASAP!"

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:17.460
--Whoa!
--When did that come down?

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:23.230
Th-There's no sound.

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:30.510
Damn it, why won't it play?

00:12:30.510 --> 00:12:33.070
This isn't right. What's going on?

00:12:34.150 --> 00:12:36.650
Sound...!

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:38.090
There was no sound.

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:40.590
The word corrosion rate is rising.

00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:42.290
It's moving so rapidly.

00:12:42.290 --> 00:12:44.430
At this rate, transit and communications

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:47.430
will fall into chaos...

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:48.920
Ugh!

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:51.170
"Sachiko: What are you doing?"

00:12:51.170 --> 00:12:52.500
"Yumi: I can't hear a thing."

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:53.870
"Sachi: Isn't this pretty bad?"

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:54.840
"Yumi: The cars and trains make no noise!

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:54.840
I can't go anywhere like this!"

00:12:56.340 --> 00:12:58.860
We must go look for Hanako!

00:13:03.140 --> 00:13:06.010
Surely, Hanako is waiting for us!

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:08.880
This old sage can tell.
Hanako is praying to save our world.

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:11.650
--Hey, why is there sound only here?
--Indeed.

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:12.890
"Shinmei Shrine

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:12.890
Hanako and Princess Kaguya"

00:13:11.650 --> 00:13:13.620
--Huh? What?
--No matter what happened,

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:16.390
--This is...
--Hanako was always praying by herself.

00:13:16.390 --> 00:13:18.360
Princess, please forgive me.

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:21.800
"Sender: Shoko Iwagami

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:21.800
Recipient: Sakurako Soda

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:21.800
Title: M.J.B.K Situation Report

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:21.800
Word corrosion rate has risen to 48%."

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:22.400
--The word corrosion is still advancing, so why?
--There is something I must tell her.

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:25.170
Let us all go search for Hanako!

00:13:25.170 --> 00:13:28.660
All I can hear is their voices.

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:30.740
"Verbalism Club Outdoor Stage Performance

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:30.740
Hanako and Princess Kaguya"

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:32.040
An M.J.B.K. that steals sound?

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:35.710
Yes, the world is quickly being robbed of its sounds.

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:38.750
But this Noh theater is the one place that's unaffected.

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:42.680
This is probably thanks to your Verbalism Ability.

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:44.750
Th-That's why the people are like this...

00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:50.520
If we defend this place, the word corrosion rate won't reach 100%.

00:13:50.520 --> 00:13:53.230
So this is our last bastion, then.

00:13:53.230 --> 00:13:56.400
Yes. For as long as we have your voices.

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:59.870
Y-You want us to keep using our voices?

00:13:59.870 --> 00:14:02.170
We'll have to keep the play going.

00:14:02.170 --> 00:14:05.040
That is our best course of action.

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:08.510
Where are you going? Don't act on your own.

00:14:08.510 --> 00:14:10.500
I will defeat the M.J.B.K.

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:16.450
Good idea. Do it while Hayato and the others buy time here.

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:18.750
Are you okay with that, Hayato?

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:20.090
Understood.

00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:21.760
U-Um...!

00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:27.130
I... I'll launch, too...

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:33.600
B-Because, I... wouldn't be any use... even if I stayed here...

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:36.100
Voice input commands cannot be used.

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:40.240
Switching system over to direct input mode.

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:43.480
Vector-1, Vector-3, prepare to launch.

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:45.140
Verbalize.

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:50.610
Verbalize.

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:53.280
Lift-off!

00:14:57.220 --> 00:15:02.900
So, basically, we have to drag out the play until the M.J.B.K.'s dealt with?

00:15:02.900 --> 00:15:07.300
But what can we do? If we follow the script, it's almost finished.

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:10.740
I'm writing in new scenes to pad out the story now.

00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:16.340
"Hanako and Princess Kaguya"

00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:13.970
If there isn't enough, ad-lib something yourselves.

00:15:13.970 --> 00:15:16.340
You're okay with me ad-libbing?

00:15:16.340 --> 00:15:20.010
Oto. Oto.

00:15:27.660 --> 00:15:29.260
Let's go, Kikogami.

00:15:29.260 --> 00:15:30.750
Y-Yes!

00:15:38.100 --> 00:15:39.590
Kikogami!

00:15:44.100 --> 00:15:45.210
I can't get in close.

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:47.610
Vector-3 has shut down.

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:50.610
Word corrosion rate has risen to 74%.

00:15:50.610 --> 00:15:53.880
The areas affected by sound loss are expanding worldwide.

00:15:57.020 --> 00:15:59.790
Verbalize.

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:03.660
Verbalize. Verbalize. Verbalize!

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:07.900
Why... can't I... do anything?

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:10.520
On stage, or in battle...

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:14.990
Look out!

00:16:17.970 --> 00:16:19.460
Avoid it!

00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:32.420
Vector-3 pilot vitals are dropping rapidly.

00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:34.650
She'll be in danger if this keeps up!

00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:41.090
Because I'm powerless...

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:46.530
N-No... I can't...

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:57.910
I can't do anything... anymore...

00:16:59.050 --> 00:17:00.540
Your voice.

00:17:03.350 --> 00:17:08.860
"Voice"

00:17:04.550 --> 00:17:09.620
Akira, what about my voice?

00:17:13.290 --> 00:17:15.020
It's not just noise.

00:17:16.730 --> 00:17:19.770
I see. Because it lacked heart,

00:17:19.770 --> 00:17:23.140
it was just noise...

00:17:19.770 --> 00:17:24.410
"Voice"

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:26.570
My voice, that is. I didn't understand.

00:17:26.570 --> 00:17:31.770
I'm always being saved by Akira.

00:17:37.920 --> 00:17:39.650
Akira.

00:17:41.720 --> 00:17:43.280
I love you!

00:17:44.390 --> 00:17:50.400
<i>Why? Why is it?</i>

00:17:50.400 --> 00:17:56.500
<i>Since the time I was a child,</i>

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:52.670
A song?

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:54.230
Kikogami.

00:17:54.230 --> 00:17:56.500
I can hear Hanako's song!

00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:59.740
My, it really is her voice!

00:17:56.500 --> 00:18:02.910
<i>I have thought, God,</i>

00:18:00.810 --> 00:18:02.580
This is better than ever.

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:05.150
What a wonderful song.

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:08.850
<i>why is everything so unfair?</i>

00:18:08.850 --> 00:18:14.760
<i>Like the mermaid who was forced to choose</i>

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:14.690
Akira, I'm right here!

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:18.760
Yes, I can hear it. Your voice.

00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:21.030
<i>between her voice and her love,</i>

00:18:18.760 --> 00:18:20.530
Sousei Gattai.

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:22.530
Reach!

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:27.630
<i>and then ultimately was able to have neither,</i>

00:18:22.530 --> 00:18:25.300
Aquarion!

00:18:27.630 --> 00:18:34.010
<i>and was turned to sea foam</i>

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:40.050
<i>A tomorrow which doesn't</i>

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:40.050
<i>promise a happy ending</i>

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:46.190
<i>is just so scary to me</i>

00:18:43.380 --> 00:18:44.950
Sei!

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:44.950
"Sei"

00:18:44.950 --> 00:18:47.120
It's a rabbit this time?!

00:18:46.190 --> 00:18:52.230
<i>So I had given up,</i>

00:18:52.230 --> 00:18:58.800
<i>but this day, today, which I spend</i>

00:18:52.230 --> 00:18:58.800
<i>with you who believed in me,</i>

00:18:53.390 --> 00:18:56.360
Incredible. I can see the sounds.

00:18:56.360 --> 00:18:57.530
I get it.

00:18:57.530 --> 00:19:01.000
If the M.J.B.K.'s sound waves and
Kikogami's song cancel each other out...

00:18:58.800 --> 00:19:02.240
<i>I will believe in as well</i>

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:03.330
Noise canceling, right?

00:19:03.570 --> 00:19:07.230
"Sing"

00:19:09.340 --> 00:19:15.080
<i>The voice I heard</i>

00:19:15.080 --> 00:19:21.760
<i>has resounded through my whole body</i>

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:34.500
<i>I'll hold the tears I can't hide</i>

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:34.500
<i>anymore tight and tell you</i>

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:26.660
I can hear!

00:19:26.660 --> 00:19:29.160
Sound is coming back!

00:19:29.160 --> 00:19:32.200
Kikogami's Verbalism Ability is being carried by her song,

00:19:32.200 --> 00:19:35.000
and it's overcoming the M.J.B.K.'s power!

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:39.840
<i>I used to worry and be hesitant,</i>

00:19:39.840 --> 00:19:46.210
<i>and I hated myself for that,</i>

00:19:43.840 --> 00:19:45.350
Is that it?

00:19:46.210 --> 00:19:52.690
<i>but I will let this voice</i>

00:19:46.210 --> 00:19:52.690
<i>you believed in resound,</i>

00:19:52.690 --> 00:19:58.530
<i>and I'll stand up once more</i>

00:19:57.860 --> 00:20:00.290
Hanako's voice has reached us!

00:20:00.290 --> 00:20:02.560
With her song, sound will return!

00:20:02.560 --> 00:20:07.270
Mille-feuille and chocolate fondue and macarons will return to this world!

00:20:07.270 --> 00:20:09.400
Hundredfold energy, kappa!

00:20:08.070 --> 00:20:14.070
<i>Those days when I was always losing things</i>

00:20:09.400 --> 00:20:12.710
My word! The kappa has revived, as well!

00:20:12.710 --> 00:20:15.310
Spread throughout the galaxy, Hanako's song!

00:20:14.070 --> 00:20:20.050
<i>I'll leave behind in yesterday</i>

00:20:19.980 --> 00:20:23.220
A voice without heart is just noise.

00:20:20.050 --> 00:20:26.050
<i>When I'm asking what I should do,</i>

00:20:23.220 --> 00:20:27.890
When I was on stage, my voice wasn't producing words.

00:20:26.050 --> 00:20:36.330
<i>I will believe in the answer</i>

00:20:26.050 --> 00:20:36.330
<i>throbbing in my chest</i>

00:20:27.890 --> 00:20:32.460
Sound infused with emotion becomes a voice and forms words.

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:36.900
Whether I'm acting or singing, it's because my heart is screaming out

00:20:36.900 --> 00:20:40.130
that my voice can reach the hearts of others.

00:20:38.470 --> 00:20:44.400
<i>The voice I heard</i>

00:20:40.130 --> 00:20:43.740
Yes, singing can be words, too!

00:20:41.640 --> 00:20:43.240
"Sound"

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:44.670
"Speak"

00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:50.780
<i>has resounded through my whole body</i>

00:20:50.780 --> 00:20:57.280
<i>I will let this voice you believed in resound,</i>

00:20:51.950 --> 00:20:56.850
Go forth, reach their hearts, O words!

00:20:57.280 --> 00:21:03.420
<i>and I will walk forward</i>

00:21:03.420 --> 00:21:09.600
<i>For tomorrow's voice, when yesterday ends,</i>

00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:15.670
<i>you can try listening to me</i>

00:21:15.670 --> 00:21:26.040
<i>So listen</i>

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:20.610
It's not over yet.

00:21:20.610 --> 00:21:24.710
O-Oh, no! W-We need to get back!

00:21:30.220 --> 00:21:32.050
I'm all dried out, kappa.

00:21:32.050 --> 00:21:34.860
Hanako... Please, come back.

00:21:34.860 --> 00:21:38.960
Princess Kaguya, we must prepare so Hanako can return at any time.

00:21:38.960 --> 00:21:43.230
Yes, let us build a Baumkuchen castle together!

00:21:50.670 --> 00:21:52.570
Hanako!

00:21:52.570 --> 00:21:59.350
♪ I'm sorry, my sister!
I've realized something, I have. ♪

00:21:59.350 --> 00:22:05.420
♪ If I have this voice, surely, ♪

00:22:05.420 --> 00:22:11.660
♪ I can do anything. ♪

00:22:11.660 --> 00:22:14.890
Now, let us all set out on a journey of salvation!

00:22:16.000 --> 00:22:17.690
Onwards!

00:22:37.420 --> 00:22:40.890
<i>Je-Je t'aime communication</i>

00:22:40.890 --> 00:22:50.890
<i>Oh, you aren't making a bit of</i> <i>eye contact with me while you talk</i>

00:22:50.930 --> 00:23:00.140
<i>Are you texting some far-off</i> <i>neighboring world or something?</i>

00:23:00.140 --> 00:23:05.270
<i>Because this isn't communication at all</i>

00:23:07.210 --> 00:23:13.750
<i>You'd at least understand that much</i>

00:23:13.750 --> 00:23:19.760
<i>even if the times suddenly changed, right?</i>

00:23:19.760 --> 00:23:23.760
<i>Give me je t'aime communication sometimes</i>

00:23:23.760 --> 00:23:27.170
<i>Look at me, answer me, and tell me</i>

00:23:27.170 --> 00:23:33.670
<i>I mean, this is practically</i> <i>like talking to a computer</i>

00:23:33.670 --> 00:23:36.680
<i>A-Adieu application</i>

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:43.320
<i>Even if it means staying lonely</i> <i>in my heart, if it'll connect us</i>

00:23:43.320 --> 00:23:49.690
<i>then, please, at least show</i> <i>your smile to me alone</i>

00:23:51.020 --> 00:23:53.790
Pamyun! Akira, what are you doing all alone?

00:23:53.790 --> 00:23:55.260
Calligraphy.

00:23:55.260 --> 00:23:58.100
Don't boys like being in groups the way girls do?

00:23:58.100 --> 00:24:00.600
There are boys who like groups and those who don't.

00:24:00.600 --> 00:24:02.670
The Verbalism Club boys just fall into the latter group.

00:24:02.670 --> 00:24:05.010
Could it be you all have no friends?!

00:24:05.010 --> 00:24:06.370
It's a bit late to be noticing that.

00:24:06.370 --> 00:24:07.370
Episode 11!

00:24:06.940 --> 00:24:09.110
"Episode 11: Flap! Bound Wings"

00:24:07.370 --> 00:24:09.110
"Flap! Bound Wings."

00:24:09.110 --> 00:24:10.870
Even if I am alone, I will watch it.
For I am the sav--
